 # 1440 - Tool list page follows the WCS page's layout
 
 - Chose: three titled groups (Tools in this setup, Time and travel, Export) over `layout::group`; the per-tool readout, which was space-padded text lines, is now a real grid with a header row (Tool, Ops, Changes, Cut, Rapid, Est (min)) and a "Setup total" line. The page moved into `tool_list_page.rs` (with `tool_table`, from `setup_pages.rs`, and `tool_list_section`, from `pages.rs`, which is far past the 400-line law).
+- Chose: both tables sit in a sideways ScrollArea, because the properties pane is narrow and the columns clipped (Ops, Rapid and Est were cut off).
 - Kept: both empty-state messages verbatim, in the same places ("No operation in this setup uses a tool yet." / "Tool list: no generated operation in this setup yet."), and every command and export as before; pinned by a structural test.
 - Dropped: equal-width `even_row` for the two export buttons. Open PR #1438 routes both through `browser_files::button`, which carries the browser build's refusal and cannot sit in an `even_row`; reshaping them now would either drop that refusal or conflict. The two existing rows are reused unchanged under an "Export" group; revisit once #1438 lands.
 - Dropped: a "Setup sheet" group of its own - the sheet export is one row.

From a164293c5ed70a79de90749f4fe66420d0776cb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:30:10 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] test(ui): pin the Tool list page's full table headers

The layout pin checked only Size and Est (min); it now asserts every
header of the tools table (T, Tool, Size, Ops) and the time readout
(Tool, Ops, Changes, Cut, Rapid, Est (min)): once each inside its group,
on one row, left to right.

Refs #1440

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
---
 .../ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_list_page.rs   | 21 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_list_page.rs b/crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_list_page.rs
index 6056f927e..38a4d58fd 100644
--- a/crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_list_page.rs
+++ b/crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_list_page.rs
@@ -22,9 +22,8 @@ fn the_tool_list_page_is_laid_out_in_groups_like_the_wcs_page() {
     assert!(tops.windows(2).all(|w| w[0] < w[1]), "groups stack top to bottom: {tops:?}");
     // The tools table (its Size column) sits in the first group, the
     // readout's table in the second.
-    assert!(rect(&harness, "Size").top() > tops[0] && rect(&harness, "Size").top() < tops[1]);
-    let est = rect(&harness, "Est (min)");
-    assert!(est.top() > tops[1] && est.top() < tops[2], "readout table under its title");
+    assert_header_row(&harness, &["T", "Tool", "Size", "Ops"], tops[0], tops[1]);
+    assert_header_row(&harness, &["Tool", "Ops", "Changes", "Cut", "Rapid", "Est (min)"], tops[1], tops[2]);
     assert!(harness.query_by_label_contains("Setup total: est").is_some(), "total line");
     // The exports come last, in order, one row each.
     let (t, s) = (rect(&harness, "Export tool list…"), rect(&harness, "Export setup sheets…"));
@@ -32,6 +31,22 @@ fn the_tool_list_page_is_laid_out_in_groups_like_the_wcs_page() {
     assert!(t.left() == s.left(), "exports share a left edge");
 }
 
+/// Every header of a table, once each between two group titles, on one
+/// row, in order left to right - so dropping or moving any column is red.
+fn assert_header_row(h: &Harness<'static, ShellUi>, headers: &[&str], lo: f32, hi: f32) {
+    let rects: Vec<egui::Rect> = headers
+        .iter()
+        .map(|l| {
+            let found: Vec<egui::Rect> =
+                h.query_all_by_label(l).map(|n| n.rect()).filter(|r| r.top() > lo && r.top() < hi).collect();
+            assert_eq!(found.len(), 1, "header {l:?} once between {lo} and {hi}: {found:?}");
+            found[0]
+        })
+        .collect();
+    assert!(rects.windows(2).all(|w| (w[0].top() - w[1].top()).abs() < 2.0), "{headers:?} on one row: {rects:?}");
+    assert!(rects.windows(2).all(|w| w[0].left() < w[1].left()), "{headers:?} left to right: {rects:?}");
+}
+
 /// With no operation in the setup, the page says what it said before the
 /// tidy, in the same places, and still offers the exports.
 #[test]
